    "title": "The Fruit That Cannot Wait and the Oil That Can: Kenya's Avocado Industry and the Case for Owning the Oil",
    "summary": "Kenya grows avocados better per hectare than Mexico and has just frozen sea exports for want of ripe fruit. Priced per kilogram of fruit rather than per kilogram of oil, crude pressing is a salvage outlet and only refined, branded oil can compete with fresh export. The margin sits abroad, and seven sequenced actions would bring it home.",
